  "notes": "{練習|れんしゅう} means practice or training — repeated effort to improve a skill. It is one of the most broadly used words for practice in Japanese.\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {練習|れんしゅう}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to practice\n- {練習|れんしゅう}⟦{問題|もんだい}→問題：00797_mondai⟧: practice problems/exercises\n- {練習|れんしゅう}⟦{試合|じあい}→試合：01601_shiai⟧: practice match/scrimmage\n- {練習|れんしゅう}⟦{中|ちゅう}→〜中：09840_chuu⟧: during practice\n- {練習|れんしゅう}⟦{量|りょう}→量：03799_ryou⟧: amount of practice\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed for both physical and mental skills: sports, musical instruments, language study, math drills, etc. The noun can stand alone ({練習|れんしゅう}⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦ある→ある：00006_aru⟧ — there's practice) or form a verb with ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧.\n\nVS. ⟦{稽古|けいこ}→稽古：00210_keiko⟧:\n{練習|れんしゅう} is the general modern word for any kind of practice. ⟦{稽古|けいこ}→稽古：00210_keiko⟧ is preferred for traditional arts (tea ceremony, martial arts, dance).",
